<title>GERMANY: German inland gasoil drops in bid for buyers.</title>
<headline>German inland gasoil drops in bid for buyers.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6900)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     33.80/34.20     20.00/20.24   34.20/34.50</p>
<p> BREMEN		33.80/34.20     20.00/20.24   34.20/34.50</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.10/33.50     19.59/19.82   33.50/33.90</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   33.70/34.10     19.94/20.17   34.00/34.40</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   33.60/34.00     19.88/20.12   34.10/34.50</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  34.20/34.60     20.24/20.47   34.80/35.20</p>
<p>German inland gas oil was lower on Tuesday despite stronger IPE gas oil futures. Traders said there was some fierce competition to shift product which prompted the morning's easier numbers to follow through into the afternoon.</p>
</text>
